    {
      "id": "lem-qftx-super-poincare-graded-jacobi",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "library": "mathematics",
      "title": "Graded Jacobi and real-form verification for the extended super-Poincare algebra",
      "reference": "items/lem-qftx-super-poincare-graded-jacobi.md",
      "design_state": "Draft authored for aqft-susy-math-foundations; full statement, dependencies, and source qualifications are in the item carrier.",
      "dependency_level": 1,
      "deps": [
        "def-qftx-super-poincare-algebra-4d",
        "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field",
        "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus"
      ],
      "dependency_roles": {
        "def-qftx-super-poincare-algebra-4d": "mathematical-premise",
        "thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field": "mathematical-premise",
        "def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus": "mathematical-premise"
      },
      "inventory_expansion_required": false,
      "statement": "For $N\\ge1$, take $S=\\mathbb C^2$, $\\dot S=\\overline S$, $\\mathfrak l=\\mathfrak{sl}(S)\\oplus\\mathfrak{sl}(\\dot S)$, $V=S\\otimes\\dot S$, $C_N=\\Lambda^2\\mathbb C^N\\oplus\\overline{\\Lambda^2\\mathbb C^N}$, even part $\\mathfrak g_{\\bar0}=\\mathfrak l\\oplus V\\oplus C_N$, and odd part $\\mathfrak g_{\\bar1}=(S\\otimes\\mathbb C^N)\\oplus(\\dot S\\otimes(\\mathbb C^N)^*)$. Give $\\mathfrak l$ its componentwise matrix commutator, its tensor action on $V$, and its fundamental actions on the two odd summands; let $C_N$ be central, $V$ abelian and trivial on the odd part. With $\\epsilon_{12}=\\epsilon_{\\dot1\\dot2}=1$, the odd brackets are $\\{Q^I_\\alpha,\\bar Q_{\\dot\\beta J}\\}=-2\\delta^I{}_J T_{\\alpha\\dot\\beta}$, $\\{Q^I_\\alpha,Q^J_\\beta\\}=2\\epsilon_{\\alpha\\beta}Z^{IJ}$, and $\\{\\bar Q_{\\dot\\alpha I},\\bar Q_{\\dot\\beta J}\\}=2\\epsilon_{\\dot\\alpha\\dot\\beta}\\bar Z_{IJ}$, with $Z^{IJ}=-Z^{JI}$ and all omitted brackets zero. Then this bracket is degree-preserving, graded-skew and satisfies the super-Jacobi identity. The conjugate-linear operation $(A,B)^*=(-\\overline B,-\\overline A)$, $Q^*=\\bar Q$, $\\bar Q^*=Q$, $T_{\\alpha\\dot\\beta}^*=T_{\\beta\\dot\\alpha}$, $(Z^{IJ})^*=\\bar Z_{IJ}$ and $(\\bar Z_{IJ})^*=Z^{IJ}$ is an involution satisfying $[x,y]^*=-(-1)^{|x||y|}[x^*,y^*]$. Consequently $\\tau(x)=-x^*$ on even elements and $\\tau(x)=i x^*$ on odd elements is an involutive conjugate-linear automorphism, and its fixed space is a real Lie superalgebra. For $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, $\\sigma^0=I_2$, $\\sigma^j$ the Pauli matrices, and $\\bar\\sigma^0=I_2$, $\\bar\\sigma^j=-\\sigma^j$, one has $\\sigma^\\mu\\bar\\sigma^\\nu+\\sigma^\\nu\\bar\\sigma^\\mu=-2\\eta^{\\mu\\nu}I_2$ and $\\det(\\sigma^\\mu p_\\mu)=-\\eta^{\\mu\\nu}p_\\mu p_\\nu$.",
      "provenance": {
        "statement": "ai-altered",
        "proof": "ai-generated"
      },
      "sources": {
        "references": [
          {
            "title": "Stephen P. Martin, A Supersymmetry Primer, version 7",
            "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/9709356v7",
            "locator": "§3.1, printed pp. 18–21, N=1 algebra derivation; the N-extended real-form and Jacobi checks below are local."
          },
          {
            "title": "S. J. Gates Jr., M. T. Grisaru, M. Roček and W. Siegel, Superspace, or One Thousand and One Lessons in Supersymmetry",
            "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0108200",
            "locator": "§§3.2–3.3, printed pp. 62–73, signed grading, super-Jacobi and extended brackets; the local convention bridge is checked here."
          }
        ]
      },
      "proof_strategy": "direct"
    },
    {
      "id": "def-qftx-unitary-super-poincare-representation",
      "kind": "definition",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "library": "mathematics",
      "title": "Positive unitary super-Poincare representation with spectral-domain covariance",
      "reference": "items/def-qftx-unitary-super-poincare-representation.md",
      "design_state": "Draft authored for aqft-susy-math-foundations; full statement, dependencies, and source qualifications are in the item carrier.",
      "dependency_level": 1,
      "deps": [
        "def-qftx-super-poincare-algebra-4d",
