+# Batch 30 authoring notes — N=1 superspace and actions
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+- Assigned pair: `qftx-susy-n1-superspace-and-actions` and its examples leaf, order 986, in `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry`.
+- The complete design at `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md` §“N=1 Superspace and Wess–Zumino/Gauge-Matter Actions” matches the current `research/plan-spec.json` rows: title, category, physics classification, pair identity, order, and required pages `qftx-susy-algebra-and-multiplets` and `qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model` agree. The plan’s empty item arrays are placeholders; the four future IDs and contracts are in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json`.
+- The plan level file records batch 30 at dependency level 3, requiring batches 19 and 29. This is page scheduling evidence; authored item levels are computed from each item's actual in-run `deps`.
+- Contract/design completeness additions: the proposed postulate rows omit the explicit chiral-superfield formulation edge; the gauge-matter candidate also names a vector multiplet without a local definition or direct non-Abelian interface. I will add those exact formulation dependencies and a local vector-superfield definition. The design calls for local off-shell invariance of the adopted actions, while the four candidate IDs list only the Wess–Zumino invariance theorem; I will also add a conditional superspace proof for the gauge-matter action. These additions preserve the specified actions and conventions; the canonical plan and other pairs remain untouched.
+- Page presentation follows the owner direction: both A/B files will contain YAML frontmatter only, with empty Markdown bodies.
+
+## Supplier inspection and current readiness
+
+- `items/def-qftx-n1-chiral-superfield.md` and its well-definedness proof `items/lem-qftx-n1-chiral-superspace-identities.md` were read in full. The definition uses smooth coefficients on flat 4D superspace, the fixed four-generator Grassmann algebra, mostly-plus metric, fixed Pauli matrices, the nilpotent chiral coordinate shift, and unique scalar/Weyl/auxiliary components. The lemma proves the covariant-derivative algebra, chiral-coordinate kernel, and preservation of chirality under the defined supercharges. Current `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` rows for both are closed and `ready`.
+- `items/def-qftx-superspace-grassmann-algebra.md` and `items/lem-qftx-grassmann-coefficient-calculus.md` were read in full. They fix the ordered Grassmann generators, left/right derivatives, conjugation, and coefficient-extraction measures; the lemma proves associativity, derivation rules, and that Berezin total derivatives integrate to zero. Both current readiness rows are closed and `ready`.
+- `items/def-qftx-super-poincare-algebra-4d.md` and `items/lem-qftx-super-poincare-graded-jacobi.md` were inspected. The applicable bridge is `eta=diag(-1,1,1,1)`, `sigma^0=I`, `bar sigma^j=-sigma^j`, and `sigma^mu bar sigma^nu + sigma^nu bar sigma^mu = -2 eta^{mu nu} I`; the current readiness rows are closed and `ready`.
+- `items/def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data.md` was inspected. It fixes a compact noncommutative group, right principal bundle, finite-dimensional unitary representations, associated bundles, and bundle sectors, with its stated `AC_omega` inheritance. Its current readiness row is closed and `ready`.
+- `items/post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model.md` and the current gauge-invariance and Euler–Lagrange proofs on its A page were inspected. The actual interface is a classical pure `SU(2)` model on oriented/time-oriented Minkowski space, `eta=(-+++)`, one selected smooth right-principal-bundle sector, no matter, `kappa(X,Y)=-2 Tr_2(XY)`, positive dimensionless `g_YM`, natural units, and the local Lorentzian action `-kappa(F wedge *F)/(2 g_YM^2)`. It makes no quantum, continuum, or empirical claim. Current live `step1Decision` checks show that all four page item readiness records are missing; the carrier status and pending prechecks alone are not treated as mathematical defects.
+- The current `qftx-susy-algebra-and-multiplets` page has two authored BPS items, each with an `escalated` readiness row because its declared `qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model` prerequisite page lacks the four current item records above. The exact N=1 algebra/superspace definitions used below are supplied directly by the ready mathematical items on `aqft-susy-math-foundations`; the planned page edge remains recorded and open.
+
+## Sources read for this A page
+
+- Stephen P. Martin, *A Supersymmetry Primer*, arXiv:hep-ph/9709356v7, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/9709356v7>. Full 160-page PDF inspected. Relevant reading: §§3.1–3.2 (off-shell chiral multiplet and interactions), §§4.1–4.9 (Grassmann integration, superspace translations, chiral/vector superfields, gauge-matter D-terms), printed pp. 18–48. The component normalization is translated to the workspace's explicit `(-+++)` and `SU(2)` connection conventions rather than imported silently.
+- Adel Bilal, *Introduction to Supersymmetry*, arXiv:hep-th/0101055v1, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0101055>. Full 83-page lecture notes inspected. Relevant reading: §4.3 (superspace variation as odd-coordinate total derivatives plus a spacetime divergence), §4.4 (real vector superfield and Wess–Zumino gauge), §§5.1–5.2 (non-Abelian field strength, gauge coupling rescaling, chiral matter representations, and component action), printed pp. 21–31. Bilal's component trace and spinor conventions differ; only the action structure is used, while the model postulate states the local normalization explicitly.
+- These two independent full-text lecture treatments support the superspace action forms and convention comparison. Local conditional derivations remain in the authored proof carriers.
+
+## Item authoring ledger
+
+No item carriers have been completed yet.
+
+## Validation and unresolved work
+
+- Final item levels planned from the currently inspected in-run suppliers: Wess–Zumino postulate 3; vector-superfield definition 4; Wess–Zumino invariance theorem 4; F-potential theorem 4; gauge-matter postulate 5; gauge-matter invariance theorem 6; cubic Wess–Zumino example 5; fundamental-doublet gauge-matter example 7.
+- The two page-level prerequisites remain open until the exact current supplier pages and their readiness edges are current. All authoring will continue conditionally on their inspected interfaces.
