+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** The adopted action, Kähler patch, holomorphic superpotential, and compactly supported component fields from the Statement.
+
+[A1] [[post-qftx-n1-wess-zumino-model]]: $S_{\mathrm{WZ}}=\int d^4x\{\int d^4\theta\,K(\bar\Phi,\Phi)+[\int d^2\theta\,W(\Phi)+\mathrm{h.c.}]\}$; the components are smooth and compactly supported; the supersymmetry parameters are constant and odd.
+
+[F1] [[def-qftx-n1-chiral-superfield]]: a chiral superfield is a smooth element of $C^\infty(\mathbb R^{1,3},\mathcal A\otimes\Lambda_4)$ with unique component expansion in the nilpotently shifted coordinate $y=x+i\theta\sigma\bar\theta$; $Q_\alpha=\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha}-i\sigma^\mu_{\alpha\dot\beta}\bar\theta^{\dot\beta}\partial_\mu$ and $\bar Q_{\dot\alpha}=-\partial^L_{\bar\theta^{\dot\alpha}}+i\theta^\beta\sigma^\mu_{\beta\dot\alpha}\partial_\mu$.
+
+[F2] [[lem-qftx-n1-chiral-superspace-identities]]: the chiral constraint is $\bar D_{\dot\alpha}\Phi=0$; in $(y,\theta,\bar\theta)$ coordinates this is independence of $\bar\theta$, and the supercharges anticommute with $\bar D$, so the supersymmetry variation preserves chirality.
+
+[F3] [[def-qftx-superspace-grassmann-algebra]]: the four ordered odd generators form a finite basis, left derivatives obey the odd Leibniz rule, and the ordered Berezin measures extract the corresponding top coefficients.
+
+## Proof
+
+**Given:** [A1] and the superfield, differential-operator, and Berezin conventions in [F1]–[F3].
+
+1.1 For any even smooth superspace function $X$, substitute the operators from [F1] into $\delta X$. Since the odd parameters are constant, the odd Leibniz rule gives $\epsilon^\alpha\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha}X=-\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha}(\epsilon^\alpha X)$ and $-\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}\partial^L_{\bar\theta^{\dot\alpha}}X=\partial^L_{\bar\theta^{\dot\alpha}}(\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}X)$. The remaining terms are ordinary spacetime derivatives, so $\delta X=-\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha}(\epsilon^\alpha X)+\partial^L_{\bar\theta^{\dot\alpha}}(\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}X)+\partial_\mu(-i\epsilon^\alpha\sigma^\mu_{\alpha\dot\beta}\bar\theta^{\dot\beta}X+i\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}\theta^\beta\sigma^\mu_{\beta\dot\alpha}X)$. [A1, F1, F3, algebra]
+
+1.2 Apply step 1.1 to the even D-term integrand $X=K(\bar\Phi,\Phi)$, whose finite nilpotent Taylor expansion is smooth. Each odd-coordinate derivative has zero top coefficient in the ordered Grassmann basis from [F3], so its Berezin integral vanishes. The spacetime-divergence term integrates to zero because the field-dependent part of $K$ is compactly supported and its constant exterior value has zero supersymmetry variation. Thus the D-term action is invariant. [A1, F3, step 1.1]
+
+2.1 For a chiral superfield $X(y,\theta)$, use $y=x+i\theta\sigma\bar\theta$ and the left-derivative rules in [F1]–[F3]. The chain rule gives $Q_\alpha=\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha}|_y$ and $\bar Q_{\dot\alpha}=-\partial^L_{\bar\theta^{\dot\alpha}}|_y+2i\theta^\beta\sigma^\mu_{\beta\dot\alpha}\partial_{y^\mu}$. Since $X$ is independent of $\bar\theta$, $\delta X=\epsilon^\alpha\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha}X+2i\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}\theta^\beta\sigma^\mu_{\beta\dot\alpha}\partial_\mu X$. [F1, F2, F3, algebra]
+
+2.2 The first term in step 2.1 integrates to zero under $d^2\theta$ by the same coefficient-extraction calculation as step 1.2. The second is the spacetime divergence $\partial_\mu(2i\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}\theta^\beta\sigma^\mu_{\beta\dot\alpha}X)$; compact support removes its boundary term. Holomorphicity and chirality make $W(\Phi)$ chiral, and complex conjugation gives the same conclusion for its antichiral conjugate. Therefore the F-term action is invariant. [A1, F1, F2, F3, step 2.1]
+
+3.1 Expand the supercharge anticommutators from [F1]. The only nonzero terms in $\{Q_\alpha,\bar Q_{\dot\beta}\}$ are $\{\partial^L_{\theta^\alpha},i\theta^\gamma\sigma^\mu_{\gamma\dot\beta}\partial_\mu\}=i\sigma^\mu_{\alpha\dot\beta}\partial_\mu$ and $\{-i\sigma^\mu_{\alpha\dot\gamma}\bar\theta^{\dot\gamma}\partial_\mu,-\partial^L_{\bar\theta^{\dot\beta}}\}=i\sigma^\mu_{\alpha\dot\beta}\partial_\mu$. Terms with two odd coordinates cancel under symmetrization, and derivatives in distinct generators anticommute by [F3]. Hence $\{Q_\alpha,\bar Q_{\dot\beta}\}=2i\sigma^\mu_{\alpha\dot\beta}\partial_\mu$ and both same-chirality anticommutators are zero. [F1, F3, algebra]
+
+3.2 By [F2], the transformations preserve the chiral constraint, so the transformed field has the unique component expansion in [F1]. Coefficient extraction is linear; therefore the operator identities in step 3.1 induce the same translation algebra on every component, including the independent auxiliary field $F^i$. No Euler–Lagrange equation was used, proving off-shell closure. [F1, F2, step 3.1] ∎
