+## Definition
+
+Use the selected smooth right-principal $SU(2)$ bundle $P\to M$ and its connection $A$ from the non-Abelian Yang–Mills model, with $M=\mathbb R^{1,3}$, $\eta=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, $\kappa(X,Y)=-2\operatorname{Tr}_2(XY)$, and positive dimensionless coupling $g_{\mathrm{YM}}$. In a local trivialization, fix Hermitian fundamental generators $t_a=\sigma_a/2$ with $\operatorname{Tr}_2(t_at_b)=\tfrac12\delta_{ab}$, write a Hermitian vector prepotential as $V=V^a t_a$, and set $A_\mu=-i g_{\mathrm{YM}} B_\mu$ when $B_\mu=B_\mu^a t_a$ is its vector component. Thus the matter covariant derivative in a unitary representation $R$ is $D_\mu=\partial_\mu

